  "_comment": [
    "Machine-readable copy of docs/MILESTONE_5.md 17.2 (Milestone 5 file ownership) and the owners of section 18's ids,",
    "read by tools/check_ownership.py --table tools/ownership_m5.json.",
    "Paths are repository-relative globs: ** spans directories, * and ? stay inside one path segment, {a,b} is either.",
    "A file belongs to a worker when it matches one of the worker's 'owns' globs and none of its 'except' globs.",
    "Everything no worker owns is the lead's (shared files change only through a request in a worker's report): the",
    "contract files of 17.1 and the shared table, which the 'except' lists name where they sit inside a worker's",
    "package (TravelService is W1's file, but its moveAcross is the lead's frozen code), combat, economy, registry,",
    "network, config, progression and holocron code, new tag files other than the ones a worker fills (18.1), the",
    "test drivers and fixtures, the check scripts, gen_sounds.py and events_m5.json.",
    "M1 to M4 files follow the M5 worker who continues their package (17.2's last rows): W1 ships and travel (M4 W3),",
    "W3 planets and the world (M4 W1), W4 story, missions, identity, dialogue, mentors and vendors (M4 W2), W6 the",
    "Choke package, every client Force class, the skill and ability code and every skill tree, W7 sabers, crafting",
    "and gear (M4 W4 and W5) except the saber duel code, which W8 takes. The other M1 to M4 Force powers, the troopers,",
    "constructs, Mandalorians, droids and creatures, the Collector's and Kaast's fights (except the music files 12.5",
    "hands to W8) and the holocrons are the lead's. An inherited test class follows the same rule.",
    "Sounds: each events_m5.json event's files belong to the worker of its feature (15.4 and 17.2): flight W1, space",
    "W2, world_m5 W3, story_m5 W4, turning W5, force_m5 W6, saber_m5 W7, enemy_m5 W8; inherited sounds follow their",
    "recipe module's owner.",
    "Phase 0 decisions here: each worker may add test helpers in gametest/m5/ named after its steps class",
    "(Flight*, Space*, Planet*, Story*, Turning*, Force*, Saber*, Foes*); W2's planet impostors and nebula go in",
    "textures/environment/space/ (W3 keeps the rest of textures/environment/), and the orbit timeline tag and any",
    "orbit timeline are W2's; a feature's new HUD or screen sprites (13.2) go in textures/gui/sprites/<folder>/",
    "(W2 space, W3 planet and world, W6 skill and mob_effect, W7 saber); W6's status effect icons may sit in",
    "textures/mob_effect/ or textures/gui/sprites/mob_effect/ (9.2's API-CHECK); W8 also owns client/boss/{raid,mentor}",
    "and KaastMusicSound, which cannot outlive KaastMusic (12.5); each worker's design doc has a docs/assets twin."
